Deployable OpenELIS distribution for {{ context_name }}.

## Quickstart

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d
```

## Contextualization

Start from the demo defaults, then replace them with deployment-specific values:

```bash
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py doctor
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py apply --profile demo --dry-run
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py apply --profile demo --non-interactive
```

The walkthrough in `docs/contextualization.md` follows the same order as
`context/config-surfaces.yml`, which is also the manifest used by the CLI.
